WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.270 --> 00:00:05.250
The War of the Ancient Dragons began thousands
of years ago...

00:00:05.250 --> 00:00:08.670
And the Erdtree Capital came under siege.

00:00:08.670 --> 00:00:13.270
Led by a gargantuan dragon named Gransax.

00:00:13.270 --> 00:00:18.480
The dragons wielded heavenly bolts of red
lightning, and so the Knights of the Erdtree

00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:23.660
learned to fortify themselves against it,
and stayed on the defensive -

00:00:23.660 --> 00:00:28.890
Until Godwyn the Golden delivered the decisive
blow.

00:00:28.890 --> 00:00:34.110
He stood before another legendary dragon,
known as Dread Fortissax.

00:00:34.110 --> 00:00:37.079
And defeated him.

00:00:37.079 --> 00:00:41.579
But instead of granting death, he showed mercy.

00:00:41.579 --> 00:00:43.470
He offered friendship.

00:00:43.470 --> 00:00:49.460
And it was with this act, that the ancient
dragons, and the Golden Order, truly became one.

00:00:52.332 --> 00:00:55.789
Years later, a dire plot was put into action.

00:00:55.789 --> 00:00:58.769
A plan to kill Godwyn, the Golden.

00:00:58.769 --> 00:01:03.899
So a fragment of the Rune of Death was stolen,
from the black blade that was designed to

00:01:03.899 --> 00:01:05.239
contain it.

00:01:05.239 --> 00:01:12.300
This fragment was then enscribed onto a set of
black knives, which the Black Knife Assassins would wield

00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:16.595
And with cloaks of silver that fooled the
eye, they snuck into the capital, and delivered

00:01:16.595 --> 00:01:20.816
the first destined death in a millenia.

00:01:24.350 --> 00:01:28.659
Godwyn should have died a clean, true death.

00:01:28.659 --> 00:01:30.460
But he did not.

00:01:30.460 --> 00:01:35.750
Instead, as the mark of death was being carved
into his flesh, it was, at that very moment,

00:01:35.750 --> 00:01:38.909
alsa being carved into another of his kin.

00:01:38.909 --> 00:01:41.020
The Lunar Princess, Ranni.

00:01:41.020 --> 00:01:46.270
Ranni got her wish, and perished in flesh
alone, which freed her soul.

00:01:46.270 --> 00:01:52.830
But Godwyn died in spirit alone, and his so
body suffered an unimaginable fate.

00:01:52.830 --> 00:01:57.829
His living corpse would spread a peculiar
brand of undeath through the Lands Between,

00:01:57.829 --> 00:01:58.969
via Deathroot.

00:01:58.969 --> 00:02:04.579
And wherever there is Deathroot, the hunters
of the dead, are sure to follow.

00:02:04.579 --> 00:02:08.080
There's no mistake, is there?

00:02:08.080 --> 00:02:11.060
Death has left its mark once again.

00:02:11.060 --> 00:02:15.680
I'm sorry, I cannot give you your proper rites...

00:02:15.680 --> 00:02:20.239
But at least you did not join Those Who Live
in Death.

00:02:20.239 --> 00:02:24.370
Your soul will return to the Erdtree, in time.

00:02:28.945 --> 00:02:32.269
Ah, a Tarnished, are you?

00:02:32.269 --> 00:02:39.170
I'm known as D. I hunt down Those Who Live
in Death, and weed their Deathroot.

00:02:39.170 --> 00:02:41.909
Heed my warning.

00:02:41.909 --> 00:02:49.433
The village here has been touched by Death.

00:02:49.433 --> 00:02:54.428
If you value your life, then go no further.

00:02:54.428 --> 00:03:00.504
The dead have long been left to wander, and
what they need, is true leadership.

00:03:00.920 --> 00:03:06.090
The mariners can call to those who live in
death, and offer them some semblance of guidance...

00:03:06.090 --> 00:03:10.879
Buuut..they make poor leaders.

00:03:10.879 --> 00:03:13.069
And even poorer fighters.

00:03:13.069 --> 00:03:18.000
So it is that the dead continue to live, without
purpose.

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:20.585
Well, well...

00:03:20.585 --> 00:03:24.580
Another fool who won't listen to reason, eh?

00:03:24.580 --> 00:03:28.230
But with a prowess for weeding Deathroot.

00:03:28.230 --> 00:03:33.338
I've spotted the mark of the centipede here in the village.

00:03:33.338 --> 00:03:36.830
An ill-omened symbol that should not be.

00:03:36.830 --> 00:03:42.855
Someone, or something, threatens the sanctity
of the Golden Order.

00:03:42.855 --> 00:03:46.334
And must be eradicated.

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:05.680
D claims to have seen the mark of the centipede
in this village.

00:04:05.680 --> 00:04:10.640
And it seems he's talking about the Deathroot
here, which is at the very heart of Those

00:04:10.640 --> 00:04:12.340
Who Live in Death.

00:04:12.340 --> 00:04:18.660
This deathroot carries the curse of the centipedal
half-wheel wound, which raises the dead from

00:04:18.660 --> 00:04:19.970
their graves.

00:04:19.970 --> 00:04:22.410
Ordering their bodies to life.

00:04:22.410 --> 00:04:23.780
Without a soul.

00:04:23.780 --> 00:04:25.000
Without guidance.

00:04:25.000 --> 00:04:26.669
And without grace.

00:04:28.126 --> 00:04:31.315
How would you like to earn the strength of
beasts?

00:04:31.315 --> 00:04:36.910
If you're inclined to hunt more of Those Who
Live in Death, and weed their Deathroot,

00:04:36.910 --> 00:04:39.430
then I'll introduce you to Gurranq.

00:04:39.430 --> 00:04:42.100
I have a matter of my own to attend to.

00:04:42.100 --> 00:04:46.060
And the beast himself wishes for someone to
take my place.

00:04:46.060 --> 00:04:47.479
What say you?

00:04:47.479 --> 00:04:49.910
Very well.

00:04:49.910 --> 00:04:51.100
Show me your map.

00:04:51.100 --> 00:04:53.410
I've marked the location for you.

00:04:53.410 --> 00:04:58.000
It will lead you to Gurranq, the beast clergyman

00:04:58.000 --> 00:05:04.250
The beastial sanctum lies past Farum Greatbridge,
deep within the Caelid Wilds.

00:05:04.250 --> 00:05:08.759
Past the vulgar militiamen, who are short,
brutal mercenaries.

00:05:08.759 --> 00:05:14.780
and the Black Blade Kindred, who are a patchwork
of champions, put back together with corpse

00:05:14.780 --> 00:05:15.780
wax.

00:05:15.780 --> 00:05:19.130
They're all here in defense..of Gurranq.

00:05:19.130 --> 00:05:21.380
Or should I say, Maliketh.

00:05:21.380 --> 00:05:27.410
He is Marika's loyal shadow, that once kept
the rune of death bound within his Black Blade.

00:05:27.410 --> 00:05:30.560
That is, until a piece of that death was stolen.

00:05:30.560 --> 00:05:35.590
Afterwards, he buried the black blade deep
within his very self..so that no one could

00:05:35.590 --> 00:05:38.413
steal it, ever again.

00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:43.660
I smell it...

00:05:43.660 --> 00:05:44.930
Death...

00:05:44.930 --> 00:05:48.000
Feed it me...

00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:54.380
Suffused with the Rune of Death, Maliketh
now hungers for deathroot - desperate to gather

00:05:54.380 --> 00:05:58.460
back what he strongly feels are the missing
parts..of himself.

00:05:58.460 --> 00:06:03.617
Tarnished...bring more...Death...

00:06:03.617 --> 00:06:08.236
I shall grant thee... eye...and claw.

00:06:09.617 --> 00:06:12.787
Feed me...more.

00:06:18.540 --> 00:06:21.650
But there was a time before
the Rune of Death was bound.

00:06:21.650 --> 00:06:24.790
And so, there were other cultures of death.

00:06:24.790 --> 00:06:30.290
Ways that were even practiced outside the
Lands Between, where the Tarnished lived in

00:06:30.290 --> 00:06:32.039
exile.

00:06:32.039 --> 00:06:36.229
Greetings, great champion called by grace.

00:06:36.229 --> 00:06:38.600
I am Fia.

00:06:38.600 --> 00:06:42.720
Circumstances have compelled my stay at the
Roundtable Hold.

00:06:42.720 --> 00:06:49.711
Great champion, would you allow me to hold
you, but briefly?

00:06:49.711 --> 00:06:54.510
Ah, my thanks.

00:06:54.510 --> 00:06:57.780
You are very warm.

00:06:57.780 --> 00:07:04.040
I was known as a Deathbed Companion, where
I come from.

00:07:04.040 --> 00:07:10.317
After I received the warmth and lifely vigour
from a number of champions,

00:07:10.317 --> 00:07:18.870
I lay with the remains of an exalted noble,
to grant him another chance at life.

00:07:18.870 --> 00:07:23.530
To do so is the purpose of my being.

00:07:23.530 --> 00:07:27.560
But before I could bear the noble into new
life,

00:07:27.560 --> 00:07:36.240
I was awakened by the guidance of grace, and
chased from my birthplace.

00:07:37.667 --> 00:07:43.206
Originally, the deathbed companions existed
to provide simple comfort to those who were

00:07:43.206 --> 00:07:44.384
dying.

00:07:44.384 --> 00:07:50.070
But at some point, it seems, it was discovered
that a deathbed companion could use the vitality

00:07:50.070 --> 00:07:54.590
of others to birth dead remains into new life.

00:07:54.590 --> 00:07:57.940
And so, the deathbed companions became a tool.

00:07:57.940 --> 00:08:04.569
A path to rebirth for the privileged - who
told the Deathbed Companions who to lie with,

00:08:04.569 --> 00:08:05.729
and when -

00:08:05.729 --> 00:08:11.449
So that one exalted being, might get a second
chance at life.

00:08:11.449 --> 00:08:18.331
Despite all that, I still wish to be a Deathbed
Companion.

00:08:18.331 --> 00:08:25.768
So please, let me hold you like this, as often
as it takes.

00:08:27.492 --> 00:08:29.690
But it's not all about you.

00:08:29.690 --> 00:08:33.490
After all, you are not the only Tarnished
that Fia lays with..

00:08:33.490 --> 00:08:37.405
And who knows what secrets are shared, in
her bedchamber?

00:08:44.301 --> 00:08:47.029
Ah, nice to meet you.

00:08:47.029 --> 00:08:48.029
The pleasure's mine.

00:08:48.029 --> 00:08:50.060
Rogier's the name.

00:08:50.060 --> 00:08:53.550
I'm looking for a little something, here in
the castle.

00:08:53.550 --> 00:08:56.910
When I'm not hotfooting it from the troops,
that is.

00:08:56.910 --> 00:09:01.740
But enough about me, what are you doing here
in Stormveil Castle?

00:09:01.740 --> 00:09:05.450
This place is bristling with Tarnished hunters,
you know.

00:09:05.450 --> 00:09:08.030
They sacrifice our kind, for grafting.

00:09:08.030 --> 00:09:14.029
Not exactly a place I'd stroll into without
a purpose in mind...

00:09:14.029 --> 00:09:18.070
Many external threats have laid waste to Stormveil
over the years,

00:09:18.070 --> 00:09:24.980
And now the castle is marred by mottled thorns,
that have worked their way through the tortured

00:09:24.980 --> 00:09:25.980
stone.

00:09:25.980 --> 00:09:31.240
The soldiers mutter that it's the curse of
grafting that causes such an affliction, but

00:09:31.240 --> 00:09:37.029
some talk of its root being something much
more sinister, hidden deep below the castle.

00:09:37.029 --> 00:09:41.100
That is why Rogier is here, on a mission of
his own.

00:09:41.100 --> 00:09:47.073
And as you square up against Godrick, he is
searching for the source of the mottled thorns.

00:09:47.073 --> 00:09:48.646
And he finds it.

00:09:48.646 --> 00:09:54.180
For the world has grown crooked, and if one
intends to put it to rights, then they'd best

00:09:54.180 --> 00:09:57.410
understand what happened to make it that way.

00:09:57.410 --> 00:09:59.798
No matter the cost.

00:10:09.339 --> 00:10:14.250
The world is slowly being taken over by the
Deathroot, that is Godwyn.

00:10:14.250 --> 00:10:21.810
For when Godwyn died, his body was buried
in the Deeproot Depths, in an esteemed position,

00:10:21.810 --> 00:10:24.149
directly below the Erdtree.

00:10:24.149 --> 00:10:30.730
This was done in accordance with the practice
of Erdtree Burial, a process which replaced

00:10:30.730 --> 00:10:32.910
Destined Death.

00:10:32.910 --> 00:10:39.380
For under Marika's Golden Order, death exists,
but it is not the end, and the roots of the

00:10:39.380 --> 00:10:45.220
Erdtree should call to all the dead, in time
- reabsorbing them into the Great Tree...where

00:10:45.220 --> 00:10:47.889
they may one day, be reborn.

00:10:47.889 --> 00:10:53.520
Godwyn, being a great hero, likely received
the burial rites that placed him as close

00:10:53.520 --> 00:10:58.279
to the Erdtree as possible...but this backfired
horrifically.

00:10:58.279 --> 00:11:04.940
For the roots would instead take up Godwyn's
cursed essence, like a tree absorbs water,

00:11:04.940 --> 00:11:10.750
and spread the mark of the centipede throughout
the Lands Between, through Deathroot.

00:11:10.750 --> 00:11:14.270
So it is, that Those Who Live in Death, were
born.

00:11:14.270 --> 00:11:17.230
...and the Hunters of the Dead, would follow.

00:11:17.230 --> 00:11:19.860
I serve the Golden Order.

00:11:19.860 --> 00:11:25.860
That I might put this crooked land to rights.

00:11:25.860 --> 00:11:30.899
Following only the guidance of the great Elden
Ring.

00:11:30.899 --> 00:11:35.149
Those Who Live in Death fall outside the principles
of the Golden Order.

00:11:35.149 --> 00:11:40.269
Their mere existence sullies the guidance
of gold.

00:11:40.269 --> 00:11:42.420
Tainting its truth.

00:11:42.420 --> 00:11:46.839
And so it is the vermin must be exterminated...

00:11:46.839 --> 00:11:51.768
Down to the very last.

00:11:53.730 --> 00:11:58.680
The Hunters of the Dead are fanatics, who
are glad to have an absolute evil to contend

00:11:58.680 --> 00:11:59.680
with.

00:11:59.680 --> 00:12:04.310
But does such an evil exist in the fundamentals
of order?

00:12:04.310 --> 00:12:08.431
Are you acquainted with a man named Rogier?

00:12:08.431 --> 00:12:12.861
You know, the piteous fellow hiding away on
the balcony?

00:12:12.861 --> 00:12:17.080
He was a formidable spellblade, in times past.

00:12:17.080 --> 00:12:19.570
Don't let his easy air deceive you.

00:12:19.570 --> 00:12:26.769
He was wise beyond his years, stout of heart
and clear of mind.

00:12:26.769 --> 00:12:32.470
Ah, so you have met D. D is an old friend.

00:12:32.470 --> 00:12:37.529
We found ourselves journeying together for a time. Bound by our exploration of Death.

00:12:37.529 --> 00:12:42.790
But their paths have since diverged, never
again to cross.

00:12:42.790 --> 00:12:47.730
Hardly an uncommon fate for two friends

00:12:47.730 --> 00:12:49.180
No more though.

00:12:49.180 --> 00:12:56.500
You see him now, ravaged by thorns, muttering
and rambling...

00:12:56.500 --> 00:13:01.630
Like he's half dead already.

00:13:01.630 --> 00:13:04.100
I can't stomach to watch.

00:13:04.100 --> 00:13:07.139
Take well the lesson, friend.

00:13:07.139 --> 00:13:11.510
That's how you end up, when seduced by Those
Who Live in Death.

00:13:11.510 --> 00:13:19.120
When grace is sullied, it rots people from
the inside.

00:13:19.120 --> 00:13:27.000
Breaks them.

00:13:27.000 --> 00:13:29.940
This is what the Golden Order has been reduced
to.

00:13:29.940 --> 00:13:30.940
Godrick.

00:13:30.940 --> 00:13:36.190
The runt of the litter, dependant on the strength
of tarnished champions.

00:13:36.190 --> 00:13:39.310
But Fia's favour is bestowed upon her consorts.

00:13:39.310 --> 00:13:42.510
It allows them to ignore any aches or pains.

00:13:42.510 --> 00:13:44.760
For in death, there is only peace.

00:13:44.760 --> 00:13:48.000
For in death, there can be no sensation.

00:13:50.763 --> 00:13:56.020
Ah, you defeated Godrick and claimed yourself
a Great Rune.

00:13:56.020 --> 00:14:00.700
Mm, looks like we both got we wanted out of
Stormveil, didn't we.

00:14:00.700 --> 00:14:02.660
Well done, friend.

00:14:02.660 --> 00:14:05.560
Always good to see you safe.

00:14:05.560 --> 00:14:06.560
So!

00:14:06.560 --> 00:14:10.079
The misshapen corpse under Stormveil?

00:14:10.079 --> 00:14:12.019
That is a sacred relic.

00:14:12.019 --> 00:14:13.600
Of the black knives plot.

00:14:13.600 --> 00:14:16.130
As that famed night of assassination is known.

00:14:16.130 --> 00:14:22.473
It happened during the Golden Age of the Erdtree,
long before the shattering of the Elden Ring.

00:14:22.473 --> 00:14:27.650
Someone stole a fragment of the Rune of Death
from Maliketh, the Black Blade.

00:14:27.650 --> 00:14:32.029
And on a bitter night, murdered Godwyn the
Golden.

00:14:35.180 --> 00:14:39.620
That was the first recorded Death of a demigod
in all history.

00:14:39.620 --> 00:14:41.240
And it became the catalyst.

00:14:41.240 --> 00:14:47.529
Soon, the Elden Ring was smashed, and thus
sprang forth the war known as the Shattering.

00:14:47.529 --> 00:14:50.350
I once wished to become a scholar, you see.

00:14:50.350 --> 00:14:54.820
I've spent many an hour scouring the archives
for knowledge of that fateful plot.

00:14:54.820 --> 00:15:01.810
And that thing is to blame for the shape i'm
in now. I urge the utmost caution.

00:15:01.810 --> 00:15:05.360
Don't disturb the corpse more than necessary.

00:15:10.235 --> 00:15:14.640
Have you ever heard of black knifeprints?

00:15:14.640 --> 00:15:20.019
Dear Rogier likes to talk of them when abed.

00:15:20.019 --> 00:15:26.687
And the ancient plot, in which the first of
the Demigods was slain.

00:15:26.687 --> 00:15:30.970
The black knives wielded by the assassins
who committed the act,

00:15:30.970 --> 00:15:38.029
along with the impressions they made, somehow
hide the truth of the conspiracy.

00:15:39.575 --> 00:15:43.010
These grand affairs are hardly my forté...

00:15:43.010 --> 00:15:49.692
But dear Rogier began to weep as he spoke...

00:15:49.692 --> 00:15:57.300
In truth I've heard tell from someone else,
about the black knifeprints that fascinate

00:15:57.300 --> 00:16:00.137
dear Rogier so.

00:16:00.137 --> 00:16:06.245
But It wouldn't be right to give this to him,
stuck as he is in the Roundtable Hold.

00:16:06.245 --> 00:16:10.300
Perhaps you could make use of it?

00:16:10.300 --> 00:16:15.720
With a crudely drawn map in hand, we can find
a living Black Knife.

00:16:15.720 --> 00:16:20.329
One of many who lurk, purposeless, in the
dark places of the Lands Between.

00:16:20.329 --> 00:16:25.588
And D is here to help you.

00:16:39.142 --> 00:16:41.790
Ahh, hello.

00:16:41.790 --> 00:16:45.830
You've been busy weeding Deathroot, I take
it.

00:16:45.830 --> 00:16:49.690
I thank you, as your brother in arms.

00:16:49.690 --> 00:16:55.670
The Black Knives were, after all, instrumental
in undoing D's beloved order.

00:16:55.670 --> 00:16:58.199
So here, he takes his revenge.

00:16:58.199 --> 00:17:02.679
..and you walk away with an imprint of a black
knife.

00:17:06.000 --> 00:17:09.790
This...is a black knifeprint!

00:17:09.790 --> 00:17:12.760
I can scarcely believe you managed to get
your hands on this!

00:17:12.760 --> 00:17:17.319
Please, I beg of you, lend me the knifeprint
for a time.

00:17:17.319 --> 00:17:28.110
I'd love nothing more than to tease out its
secrets. Half my body has been suffused with death. I'm certain it will help me see. 

00:17:28.110 --> 00:17:34.495
Though only a fragment, a very specific ritual
had to be performed to impart the power of

00:17:34.495 --> 00:17:39.699
Traces of the one who performed the rite are
sure to remain in the imprint...

00:17:39.699 --> 00:17:42.815
Truly, you have my thanks.  

00:17:42.991 --> 00:17:49.791
Time can move rather slowly, stuck here, you know. A little conversation goes a long way. 

00:18:01.414 --> 00:18:04.190
So Rogier continues his investigation.

00:18:04.190 --> 00:18:09.916
And you continue to seek out Deathroot, waiting
for the truth of things to be revealed.

00:18:09.916 --> 00:18:16.850
You are, basically, put to good use by everyone around you.

00:18:17.050 --> 00:18:19.350
I am pleased to see you again.

00:18:19.350 --> 00:18:30.799
Would you like me to hold you? Come closer. You are so very warm.

00:18:30.799 --> 00:18:35.570
I heard that you lent a hand to dear Rogier.

00:18:35.570 --> 00:18:37.900
He seemed positively elated.

00:18:37.900 --> 00:18:41.120
He must be possessed of great mental fortitude.

00:18:41.120 --> 00:18:48.340
It anchors his will, and sustains him, despite
his grievous wounds.

00:18:48.340 --> 00:18:51.438
You truly are a champion.

00:18:51.438 --> 00:18:56.435
To dear Rogier, and myself, too.

00:18:56.435 --> 00:19:00.860
My dear,
Might I ask something of you?

00:19:00.860 --> 00:19:06.270
Could you please find the owner of this dagger,
and return it to them?

00:19:06.270 --> 00:19:10.370
A certain person gave it to me, as a gift.

00:19:10.370 --> 00:19:12.700
It's a very precious thing.

00:19:12.700 --> 00:19:17.110
It must have a special place in the owner's
heart.

00:19:17.110 --> 00:19:21.730
So I would like for the original owner to
have it back.

00:19:21.730 --> 00:19:23.799
If you wouldn't mind...

00:19:23.799 --> 00:19:29.800
This Weathered Dagger was once a special weapon
of gold and silver intertwined..except now

00:19:29.800 --> 00:19:34.409
it has been worn down, and marred by a black
gash.

00:19:34.409 --> 00:19:38.169
It's natural to think that this weapon belongs
to D.

00:19:38.169 --> 00:19:42.370
But then..why didn't Fia give it back to him
herself?

00:19:42.370 --> 00:19:45.970
Well, what have we here?

00:19:45.970 --> 00:19:50.490
How did you get your hands on that dagger?

00:19:50.490 --> 00:19:53.591
...
Well.

00:19:53.710 --> 00:19:56.057
That hardly matters.

00:19:56.057 --> 00:19:58.570
I know very well whose dagger it is.

00:19:58.570 --> 00:20:01.580
Why don't I return it to them for you?

00:20:01.580 --> 00:20:05.090
Good work, bringing this to me.

00:20:05.090 --> 00:20:09.190
It's almost as if they're playing a game with
the dagger.

00:20:09.190 --> 00:20:13.800
Arguing over whose heart it truly deserves
to be buried within.

00:20:16.130 --> 00:20:18.870
And it's a game that D ends up losing.

00:20:18.870 --> 00:20:25.370
For Fia developed a sorcery to oppose the
Roundtable Hold - a mist of deathblight, that

00:20:25.370 --> 00:20:28.370
is only effective against the Tarnished.

00:20:28.370 --> 00:20:34.511
Especially if they confront you in a small,
enclosed room.

00:20:41.556 --> 00:20:47.070
Finally, it is returned to its rightful place.

00:20:47.070 --> 00:20:51.660
The stolen hallowbrand, of the exalted noble.

00:20:51.660 --> 00:20:56.130
And now, I must bid you goodbye as well.

00:20:56.130 --> 00:21:00.862
Though I ask you deliver this message to the
Roundtable Hold.

00:21:00.862 --> 00:21:05.778
I am Fia, Deathbed Companion.

00:21:05.778 --> 00:21:09.520
Hark, Roundtable.

00:21:09.520 --> 00:21:13.750
Disturb not the Death of Godwyn, the exalted.

00:21:13.750 --> 00:21:17.616
We, who humbly live in Death...

00:21:17.616 --> 00:21:23.350
Live in waiting, to one day welcome our Lord.

00:21:23.350 --> 00:21:26.884
What right does anyone have to object?

00:21:26.884 --> 00:21:30.000
Our Lord will rise.

00:21:30.000 --> 00:21:33.645
The Lord of the many, and the meek.

00:21:36.647 --> 00:21:43.430
All this time, Fia was getting closer to recovering
the Hallowbrand that D stole from Godwyn.

00:21:43.430 --> 00:21:45.870
For this hallowbrand is the key.

00:21:45.870 --> 00:21:50.970
It's the cursemark that the black knives carved
to split death in half..which started all

00:21:50.970 --> 00:21:53.029
of this in the first place -

00:21:53.029 --> 00:21:55.130
And Fia has a use for it.

00:21:55.130 --> 00:21:58.370
While D is dead.

00:22:00.807 --> 00:22:03.093
But D is also alive.

00:22:03.093 --> 00:22:06.730
For Devin and Darian are the inseparable twins.

00:22:06.730 --> 00:22:11.920
They are of two bodies, and two minds, but
one single soul.

00:22:11.920 --> 00:22:18.529
Supposedly, they were reviled by many - but
they found solace within the Golden Order,

00:22:18.529 --> 00:22:22.201
which accepted their duality of the self.

00:22:22.201 --> 00:22:25.610
They even had armaments forged to represent
their state of being..

00:22:25.610 --> 00:22:33.570
An inseperable sword, and a twinned suit of
armor, that long to find their way back to

00:22:33.570 --> 00:22:36.310
the other D, who yet lives.

00:22:36.310 --> 00:22:42.970
Devin slumbers in the Eternal City, tormented
by deathblight - where he is said to have

00:22:42.970 --> 00:22:48.840
stood before the Prince of Death, suggesting
he was the one who carved the cursemark from

00:22:48.840 --> 00:22:50.120
Godwyn's flesh.

00:22:50.120 --> 00:22:57.789
Perhaps he even used a Weathered Dagger..
that was then mockingly gifted to a rotten

00:22:57.789 --> 00:22:59.200
witch.

00:22:59.200 --> 00:23:03.279
Setting into motion the events that would
lead to his brother Darian's death.

00:23:27.049 --> 00:23:28.900
The mariners are a joke.

00:23:28.900 --> 00:23:32.770
Making your hunt for the spreading Deathroot,
an easy one.

00:23:32.770 --> 00:23:38.620
It shows up in Limgrave, in Liurnia - even
in the mountaintops of the giants.

00:23:38.620 --> 00:23:46.980
And is most common wherever there is stagnant
water, which reflects corruption, and defilement.

00:23:46.980 --> 00:23:53.549
Infecting all manner of creatures, who meet
their end sporting distorted pustules of Godwyn's

00:23:53.549 --> 00:23:55.179
own visage.

00:23:55.179 --> 00:23:58.580
Deathroot even starts to get the better of
Marika's own shadow.

00:23:58.580 --> 00:24:03.159
After all, in the end, what we're feeding
him is now much more than just the missing

00:24:03.159 --> 00:24:06.150
fragments of the Rune of Death.

00:24:06.150 --> 00:24:07.815
Something has changed. 

00:24:07.815 --> 00:24:12.501
mmmm
Strange...

00:24:12.501 --> 00:24:15.060
There's something else...

00:24:15.060 --> 00:24:18.410
I must consume more!

00:24:30.749 --> 00:24:34.784
&lt;growl&gt;
Put it away.

00:24:34.784 --> 00:24:43.488
I won't forget...again...
mine appetite...

00:24:43.488 --> 00:24:46.340
My sin...

00:24:46.340 --> 00:24:53.430
I must consume more.

00:24:53.430 --> 00:24:53.930
It is...

00:25:04.572 --> 00:25:09.642
It is all...consumed.

00:25:09.790 --> 00:25:14.960
Still, I am not sated...

00:25:14.960 --> 00:25:17.732
Not nearly sated...

00:25:17.732 --> 00:25:21.617
Marika...

00:25:21.647 --> 00:25:26.579
Is this...what it is...to sin?

00:25:26.639 --> 00:25:33.641
Will things...never be the same...again?

00:25:37.178 --> 00:25:44.930
Tarnished, my thanks for thy long labour.

00:25:44.930 --> 00:25:53.771
But I have done all that I can in this land.

00:25:53.771 --> 00:26:01.747
Henceforth, mine appetite shall be my sole
companion.

00:26:01.747 --> 00:26:04.384
Farewell.

00:26:14.966 --> 00:26:16.970
Ahh, hello.

00:26:16.970 --> 00:26:18.610
I was hoping to see you.

00:26:18.610 --> 00:26:20.460
My examination is complete.

00:26:20.460 --> 00:26:23.270
Here's the knifeprint back, with my thanks.

00:26:23.270 --> 00:26:28.210
Now, I have a fairly good idea who performed
the rite upon the blade.

00:26:28.210 --> 00:26:32.950
The person who orchestrated the Night of the
Black Knives.

00:26:32.950 --> 00:26:34.600
Lunar Princess Ranni.

00:26:34.600 --> 00:26:40.460
One of the children born to King Consort Radagon
and his first wife, Renalla.

00:26:40.460 --> 00:26:44.240
Demigod and sister to General Radahn and Praetor
Rykard.

00:26:44.240 --> 00:26:48.400
Her's was the name I discovered in the imprint.

00:26:48.400 --> 00:26:51.620
If Ranni truly is the one who plotted that
fateful night,

00:26:51.620 --> 00:26:56.300
then she should bear the cursemark of Destined
Death somewhere upon her flesh.

00:26:56.300 --> 00:26:59.830
I would like you to procure it for me.

00:26:59.830 --> 00:27:02.130
And then all will be laid bare.

00:27:02.130 --> 00:27:04.720
I will have the answers I have sought for
so long.

00:27:04.720 --> 00:27:09.039
Do you know of Those Who Live in Death?

00:27:09.039 --> 00:27:11.929
These souls have committed no offence.

00:27:11.929 --> 00:27:17.669
They have every right to life, only, they
happened to touch upon a flaw in the Order.

00:27:17.669 --> 00:27:21.750
By D's account, these defiled fiends must
be expunged.

00:27:21.750 --> 00:27:29.809
But truth be told, I seek the cursemark to
save them.

00:27:29.809 --> 00:27:34.360
If we're looking for someone to blame in this
mess, where do we land?

00:27:34.360 --> 00:27:39.049
Does the guilt lie with Those Who Live in
Death, who touched Deathroot?

00:27:39.049 --> 00:27:42.080
Or Godwyn, who spawned it?

00:27:42.080 --> 00:27:46.970
Or should we blame Ranni, who thought up the
plot in the first place?

00:27:46.970 --> 00:27:51.549
Personally, I think any fault goes further
back.

00:27:51.549 --> 00:27:57.970
To Marika, who, in her hubris, thought that
she could free the world from death.

00:27:57.970 --> 00:28:02.169
Death, and life, should never have been separated.

00:28:02.169 --> 00:28:07.340
A fact that is more clear now, than ever.

00:28:07.340 --> 00:28:08.440
Hmm.

00:28:08.440 --> 00:28:10.659
Maybe I should tell you.

00:28:10.659 --> 00:28:14.289
Lately, I feel I'm on the precipice...

00:28:14.289 --> 00:28:19.520
Of falling into a deep...fathomless slumber.

00:28:19.520 --> 00:28:23.940
And I have an inkling it could spell trouble
for you, somehow.

00:28:23.940 --> 00:28:28.000
So I just wanted to get the apology out of
the way, beforehand.

00:28:28.000 --> 00:28:31.075
Since you're so scary and all.

00:28:37.555 --> 00:28:50.800
Off..er her c-curse...m-mark
Fi…a's… fi…a's…

00:28:50.800 --> 00:28:53.466
T-to...

00:28:53.466 --> 00:29:04.879
G-god... wyn
A…fu-full...circle

00:29:04.879 --> 00:29:10.429
F-forms…a…r...rune...

00:29:30.380 --> 00:29:35.900
So whoever can obtain two halves of the cursemark,
can form a rune.

00:29:36.000 --> 00:29:41.010
And with his dying breath, Rogier hints that
Fia might be able to use this.

00:29:41.010 --> 00:29:46.820
And a letter scrawled by Rogier on his deathbed
tells one last thing.

00:29:46.820 --> 00:29:49.799
It's that D had a twin brother.

00:29:49.799 --> 00:29:55.440
And that the other D might be found in an
aqueduct, beside the Eternal City of Nokron.

00:29:55.440 --> 00:30:01.140
Rogier implores us to put his friend to rest,
and reunite the twins.

00:30:01.140 --> 00:30:06.040
Which we do...by returning D's armor.

00:30:06.040 --> 00:30:09.186
Ah, aah...

00:30:09.186 --> 00:30:11.790
D-da...ri...

00:30:11.790 --> 00:30:15.167
Ngh...nnngh...

00:30:15.167 --> 00:30:21.360
Rogier goes on to reveal that Devin stood
before Godwyn, not far beyond this spot.

00:30:21.360 --> 00:30:25.460
And indeed Devin, and the dagger, were deathblighted
here.

00:30:25.460 --> 00:30:27.299
So we travel a little farther.

00:30:27.299 --> 00:30:34.590
Upwards, to a nameless city, overtaken by
roots, and Godwyn himself.

00:30:34.590 --> 00:30:40.085
Oh, Lord Godwyn...

00:30:40.085 --> 00:30:46.870
My poor, sweet lordling should have died a
true death.

00:30:46.870 --> 00:30:54.790
A scion of the golden bough, sentenced to
live in Death...

00:30:54.790 --> 00:31:01.323
How could such a thing come to be...

00:31:04.415 --> 00:31:10.910
Here, Fia finally lies with Godwyn, the Prince
of Death..defending his being with the sapped

00:31:10.910 --> 00:31:15.919
strength of every hero who lay with her.

00:31:15.919 --> 00:31:22.750
Including, of course, The famed spellblade,
Rogier.

00:32:01.117 --> 00:32:02.880
Ah...there you are.

00:32:02.880 --> 00:32:05.247
I knew you would come.

00:32:05.247 --> 00:32:07.260
What is it you intend?

00:32:07.260 --> 00:32:09.820
To deny us, and our ways?

00:32:09.820 --> 00:32:13.644
Like the dogmatic brutes of the Golden Order?

00:32:16.200 --> 00:32:19.340
You are an odd one.

00:32:19.340 --> 00:32:22.340
I am the guardian of Those Who Live in Death.

00:32:22.340 --> 00:32:26.860
They call me a foul and rotten witch.

00:32:26.860 --> 00:32:29.433
Yet you still wish to be held by me?

00:32:37.289 --> 00:32:41.450
This...is the other hallowbrand.

00:32:41.450 --> 00:32:43.828
How did you...

00:32:43.828 --> 00:32:45.602
Oh, my utmost thanks.

00:32:45.602 --> 00:32:50.809
With this, Godwyn can take his rightful place
as First of the Dead.

00:32:50.809 --> 00:32:54.470
And claim a second, illustrious life.

00:32:54.470 --> 00:32:58.769
You are my-- our true champion.

00:32:58.769 --> 00:33:01.220
And though I can't be of any use to you.

00:33:01.220 --> 00:33:03.280
Can I hold you tight?

00:33:03.280 --> 00:33:05.370
If only for a moment.

00:33:13.370 --> 00:33:16.210
I will soon lay with Godwyn.

00:33:16.210 --> 00:33:19.140
And it will surely stir within me.

00:33:19.140 --> 00:33:24.779
the new life of the golden prince, and first
Dead of the demigods,

00:33:24.779 --> 00:33:27.360
as the rune of Those Who Live in Death.

00:33:27.360 --> 00:33:31.740
Please, do one thing for me.

00:33:31.740 --> 00:33:36.770
Brandish this child, my rune, and take for
yourself the throne.

00:33:36.770 --> 00:33:41.810
Stay the persecution of Those Who Live in
Death.

00:33:41.810 --> 00:33:44.750
By becoming our Elden Lord.

00:33:44.750 --> 00:33:48.510
This is goodbye, my dear.

00:33:48.510 --> 00:33:51.899
But I am satisfied.

00:33:51.899 --> 00:33:56.750
I choose to lie with Godwyn of my own will.

00:33:56.750 --> 00:33:59.857
Not the remains of one chosen for me.

00:33:59.857 --> 00:34:01.992
And I will bear a child.

00:34:01.992 --> 00:34:04.414
Who will inherit your warmth, too.

00:34:04.414 --> 00:34:11.753
What greater blessing could there be, but
to be born a Deathbed Companion?

00:34:11.753 --> 00:34:16.803
Now Fia can fulfil her purpose, and initiate a rebirth.

00:34:16.803 --> 00:34:22.192
A gestated rune that tells the broken story of those who live in death.

00:34:22.192 --> 00:34:26.050
So Fia lies with Godwyn, and she dreams.

00:34:26.050 --> 00:34:30.359
But it's within this dream, that we realise
there is something lurking inside the Prince

00:34:30.359 --> 00:34:31.359
of Death.

00:34:31.359 --> 00:34:37.400
A being who, even after all this time, never
once stopped fighting against the death in

00:34:37.400 --> 00:34:38.790
their companion.

00:34:38.790 --> 00:34:43.073
They are the last thing that stands between
Godwyn, and his new life..

00:34:43.073 --> 00:34:45.381
And now they refuse to let go.

00:34:45.500 --> 00:34:47.030
For Godwyn was a friend.

00:34:47.030 --> 00:34:51.433
And they were the great ancient dragon, Dread
Fortissax.

00:36:21.513 --> 00:36:28.500
Finally, you can bring the entire broken cursemark
itself, into order.

00:36:28.500 --> 00:36:35.380
The Mending Rune of the Death Prince, which
enables his bastardisation of life, to become

00:36:35.380 --> 00:36:38.220
an official part of Death's Story.

00:36:38.220 --> 00:36:46.680
But first, you have to burn down the Erdtree,
and walk alongside flame to meet the road

00:36:46.680 --> 00:36:48.780
of destined death.

00:36:48.780 --> 00:36:51.410
Which leads to Faram Azula.

00:36:51.410 --> 00:36:55.432
A broken city, floating outside of time.

00:37:06.223 --> 00:37:11.040
...and against all logic, deathroot now grows
here too.

00:37:11.040 --> 00:37:18.960
Turns out, nowhere is safe from its touch.
Even in Faram Azula, where the true Rune of

00:37:18.960 --> 00:37:22.490
Death is still protected -

00:37:22.490 --> 00:37:28.600
by none other than Maliketh - who masqueraded
as Gurranq, so that you might feed him deathroot.

00:37:28.600 --> 00:37:37.510
And help him to achieve the one and only task
that Marika saw fit to entrust him with.

00:37:46.606 --> 00:37:49.796
Witless Tarnished...

00:37:50.925 --> 00:37:53.906
Why covet Destined Death?

00:37:53.906 --> 00:37:57.705
Tis no matter.

00:37:57.705 --> 00:38:00.442
I hereby vow,

00:38:00.442 --> 00:38:09.370
that Destined Death shall not be stolen again.

00:38:09.370 --> 00:38:10.960
Cower.

00:38:10.960 --> 00:38:18.200
Before Maliketh, Marika's Black Blade.

00:39:16.622 --> 00:39:23.666
Marika...why...
wouldst thou...gull me?

00:39:25.174 --> 00:39:29.291
Why...shatter...

00:39:41.241 --> 00:39:43.069
Ha!

00:39:43.069 --> 00:39:47.370
Prince of Death, take a good long look!

00:39:47.370 --> 00:39:49.609
See the wrath of the Golden Order!

00:39:49.609 --> 00:39:54.040
The Order's justice, writ in blood!

00:39:54.040 --> 00:40:00.220
This is what's become of your precious witch!

00:40:00.220 --> 00:40:05.150
No more children can be got from this useless
flesh!

00:40:05.150 --> 00:40:08.875
This is a proper death, O prince.

00:40:08.875 --> 00:40:13.865
Behold, your mother is dead!

00:40:13.950 --> 00:40:17.940
Heh heh heh heh...

00:40:19.520 --> 00:40:21.710
This is revenge, you witch!

00:40:21.710 --> 00:40:25.069
And you, you ghoul!

00:40:25.069 --> 00:40:26.920
This is the wrath of D!

00:40:31.230 --> 00:40:32.230
Ah.

00:40:32.736 --> 00:40:33.706
Hello.

00:40:33.914 --> 00:40:37.287
The 
rotten witch is dead.

00:40:37.287 --> 00:40:39.707
The Golden Order, unsullied.

00:40:40.520 --> 00:40:45.000
Now I can look my brother Darian in the eye.

00:40:45.000 --> 00:40:49.369
Honeyed rays of gold, deliver my spirit.

00:40:49.369 --> 00:40:54.930
Darian....Honeyed rays of gold, deliver m-

00:40:54.930 --> 00:40:58.630
Ahh, don't you dare.

00:41:00.354 --> 00:41:04.154
Unless you want to die like a dog.

00:41:04.773 --> 00:41:06.368
Very well.

00:41:09.248 --> 00:41:10.691
Die.

00:41:10.929 --> 00:41:11.905
Die.

00:41:13.285 --> 00:41:15.004
DIE.

00:41:20.611 --> 00:41:23.692
(laughs)
Then you are a blight.

00:41:23.692 --> 00:41:30.717
A defiler of the Golden Order and murderer
of my brother.

00:41:32.977 --> 00:41:35.240
I'll grind your corpse into th-

00:41:58.419 --> 00:42:02.739
(laughs)

00:42:05.820 --> 00:42:11.550
Forgive me, D-arian...

00:42:11.550 --> 00:42:15.870
Darian...

00:42:31.118 --> 00:42:35.450
As a Deathbed Companion, Fia had no choice
but to lie with others.

00:42:35.450 --> 00:42:39.660
Until the guidance of grace led her back to
the Lands between.

00:42:39.660 --> 00:42:44.319
Where she used her chambers in the Roundtable
Hold to great effect.

00:42:44.319 --> 00:42:45.830
Biding her time.

00:42:45.830 --> 00:42:49.599
Listening to the secrets told to her in private.

00:42:49.599 --> 00:42:52.390
Until she could use the strength of champions
to speak for others.

00:42:52.390 --> 00:42:55.866
For the downtrodden, who had no champion.

00:42:55.866 --> 00:42:58.866
But soon, they will.

00:43:36.304 --> 00:43:41.369
Now, Fia has finally lain with the remains
of one she chose.

00:43:41.369 --> 00:43:45.690
So that she might gestate a new beginning:
called the Mending Rune of Those Who Live

00:43:45.690 --> 00:43:46.910
in Death.

00:43:46.910 --> 00:43:51.910
A gift to the the undead, who were born at
the very end of an age.

00:43:51.910 --> 00:44:02.725
Duskborn, before the sun rises once more,
in a land where they no longer have to hide.

00:44:05.400 --> 00:44:11.770
The fallen leaves tell a story.

00:44:11.770 --> 00:44:18.559
Of how a Tarnished became Elden Lord.

00:44:18.559 --> 00:44:23.140
In our home, across the fog.

00:44:23.140 --> 00:44:26.770
The Lands Between.

00:44:26.770 --> 00:44:37.387
Our seed will look back upon us, and recall:
The Age of the Duskborn.

